# `best = value < best ? value : best` on an element that the loop has just loaded is a comparison and a select, which no branch predictor has to guess. The loop is unrolled eight times, and its only branch is the test of the counter.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 8
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# REPEAT: turn = 1..8
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[value%(turn)]] = Load(b@{{*}}Reads:TypedArrayElements
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isSmaller%(turn)]] = LessThan(b@[[value%(turn)]], b@[[best%(turn)]], {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@{{*}} = Select(b@[[isSmaller%(turn)]], b@[[value%(turn)]], b@[[best%(turn)]]
# END REPEAT
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 18, patchpoints: 8, {{*}} steps by 8
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 19, patchpoints: 8, {{*}} steps by 8
